  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}\u20613x-2{sin}^{2}\u20613x+6x)\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u20612\\theta ={cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta -{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =3x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u20616x={cos}^{2}\u20613x-{sin}^{2}\u20613x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}\u20613x-2{sin}^{2}\u20613x+6x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}(2\\operatorname{cos}\u20616x+6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2}{6}\\operatorname{sin}\u20616x+\\frac{6}{2}{x}^{2})|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}\u20616x+3{x}^{2})|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3\\pi )+3{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}]-[\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\pi )+3{(\\frac{\\pi }{6})}^{2}] \\\\  & =3(\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{36}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2{\\pi }^{2}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
